Phoebe, come on.

487
00:23:53.600 --> 00:23:54.601
Are you hungry?

488
00:23:56.019 --> 00:23:57.020
Little tradition.

489
00:23:59.481 --> 00:24:01.066
Let battle commence.

490
00:24:01.525 --> 00:24:02.734
Ted Lasso?

491
00:24:02.818 --> 00:24:05.195
-Hey there, Ollie.
-Leave it out. What are you doing here?

492
00:24:05.279 --> 00:24:06.738
Well, I mean, you invited me, remember?

493
00:24:06.822 --> 00:24:08.824
I invite every person
who's been in my car.

494
00:24:08.907 --> 00:24:11.368
Hey, Ollie. This is my friend Trent.

495
00:24:11.451 --> 00:24:13.495
-Trent, this is my buddy Ollie.
-Pleased to meet you.

496
00:24:13.579 --> 00:24:15.789
Congrats. You both just met a cool person.

497
00:24:16.331 --> 00:24:18.041
Right, gentlemen.
You know what you're having?

498
00:24:18.625 --> 00:24:20.502
Yeah. Well, you know,
whatever the chef recommends.

499
00:24:20.586 --> 00:24:24.047
That would be my father-in-law.
Are you okay with a little bit of spice?

500
00:24:24.131 --> 00:24:26.466
Have him make it for us
like we're a couple members of the family.

501
00:24:27.050 --> 00:24:28.135
You're a brave man.

502
00:24:31.138 --> 00:24:33.015
Oh, man. Mad respect.

503
00:24:33.098 --> 00:24:35.267
That might not be the wisest of choices.

504
00:24:36.727 --> 00:24:37.978
Here you go, boys.

505
00:24:38.896 --> 00:24:40.147
-Dig in.
-Can't wait.

506
00:24:40.230 --> 00:24:42.316
The smell's already deep inside my brain.

507
00:24:42.399 --> 00:24:44.943
-Gonna love it.
-I appreciate it.

508
00:24:45.027 --> 00:24:47.738
I can't imagine
they have good Indian food in Kansas.

509
00:24:47.821 --> 00:24:50.365
I have no idea.
I've never had Indian food.

510
00:25:02.127 --> 00:25:03.712
Wow, that-- I mean, that's hot.

511
00:25:03.795 --> 00:25:06.840
Oh boy, oh boy, oh boy.
Feel like I'm about to breathe fire.

512
00:25:08.842 --> 00:25:09.927
I don't think I can eat that.

513
00:25:10.802 --> 00:25:13.013
What? No, no, no. Come on now.
We gotta put a decent dent in this,

514
00:25:13.096 --> 00:25:15.390
otherwise we're gonna embarrass Ollie
in front of his family.

515
00:25:15.933 --> 00:25:19.061
-No, really, I can't.
-Come on, just dump it on my plate.

516
00:25:21.021 --> 00:25:22.648
Yeah, yeah. You're good.

517
00:25:22.731 --> 00:25:25.317
So, if you love Kansas so much,
why did you--

518
00:25:26.109 --> 00:25:30.197
Why did you leave to coach a sport
you can barely-- you know anything about?

519
00:25:30.280 --> 00:25:31.281
Was it just the money?

520
00:25:31.865 --> 00:25:33.575
Wait, I'm supposed to be getting paid?

521
00:25:33.659 --> 00:25:34.826
Are you enjoying the food?

522
00:25:35.285 --> 00:25:37.120
Tell your father-in-law it's perfect.

523
00:25:37.663 --> 00:25:39.081
Dad! He says it's perfect!

524
00:25:41.041 --> 00:25:43.794
Ted. What you're doing is irresponsible.

525
00:25:44.253 --> 00:25:46.255
This club actually means something
to this town.

526
00:25:46.839 --> 00:25:47.881
I know that.

527
00:25:47.965 --> 00:25:48.966
I do.

528
00:25:49.591 --> 00:25:51.134
Trent, what do you love?

529
00:25:53.220 --> 00:25:54.221
Is it writing?

530
00:25:55.389 --> 00:25:56.223
-Yes.
-Yeah.

531
00:25:56.306 --> 00:25:57.808
Well, good, 'cause you're darn good at it.

532
00:25:58.225 --> 00:25:59.434
-Thank you.
-You're welcome.

533
00:25:59.518 --> 00:26:01.436
Me? I love coaching.

534
00:26:02.020 --> 00:26:03.146
Now, I'm gonna say this again

535
00:26:03.230 --> 00:26:05.774
just so you didn't think
it was a mistake the first time I said it.

536
00:26:05.858 --> 00:26:08.026
For me,
success is not about the wins and losses.

537
00:26:08.610 --> 00:26:11.280
It's about helping these young fellas
be the best versions of themselves

538
00:26:11.363 --> 00:26:12.364
on and off the field.

539
00:26:12.865 --> 00:26:14.283
And it ain't always easy, Trent,

540
00:26:14.366 --> 00:26:18.036
but neither is growing up
without someone believing in you.

541
00:26:19.705 --> 00:26:20.831
Let me ask you this.

542
00:26:21.874 --> 00:26:23.542
Is my tongue still in my mouth?

543
00:26:23.625 --> 00:26:26.044
'Cause I am about to hallucinate
from all the heat here.

544
00:26:29.047 --> 00:26:30.048
I really should go.

545
00:26:31.175 --> 00:26:33.552
-Deadlines and all.
-Hey, gotta do the work.

546
00:26:33.635 --> 00:26:34.887
Hey, I'll say this though.

547
00:26:34.970 --> 00:26:37.139
I really enjoyed getting to
spend this time with you, Trent.

548
00:26:38.265 --> 00:26:39.474
You actually mean that, don't you?

549
00:26:41.894 --> 00:26:42.811
Yeah.

550
00:26:44.188 --> 00:26:45.564
-Thank you.
-You're welcome.

551
00:26:46.106 --> 00:26:46.940
You all right?

552
00:26:48.025 --> 00:26:50.027
Normally, one dish is plenty,

553
00:26:50.110 --> 00:26:52.779
but we know how
you Americans like to eat, innit?

554
00:26:53.405 --> 00:26:54.406
Let's do it, huh?

555
00:26:55.449 --> 00:26:56.575
Try that one.

556
00:27:03.373 --> 00:27:06.126
-Beautiful, right?
-It's beyond beautiful. It's hot.

557
00:27:08.837 --> 00:27:10.881
"Mrs. Which's voice was grave.

558
00:27:11.673 --> 00:27:13.175
'What do you understand?'

559
00:27:14.051 --> 00:27:15.469
'That it has to be me.

560
00:27:16.303 --> 00:27:17.763
Can't be anyone else.'"

561
00:27:22.267 --> 00:27:23.352
Fuck!

562
00:27:24.144 --> 00:27:26.146
That's a bad word, Uncle Roy.

563
00:27:26.230 --> 00:27:27.898
Mind your own business, Phoebe.

564
00:27:32.277 --> 00:27:33.278
Be good.

565
00:27:40.786 --> 00:27:43.997
-Yes?
-I have an advance copy of the article.

566
00:27:45.582 --> 00:27:48.627
-Read it to me.
-Title: "Wayward Ted."

567
00:27:49.336 --> 00:27:52.422
<i>"Whatever you think of Ted Lasso
as a football coach,</i>

568
00:27:52.506 --> 00:27:56.218
<i>I assure you,
the truth is harder to swallow."</i>

569
00:27:56.301 --> 00:27:59.012
-Hey, how you doing?
-Good. How's your nose, Coach?

570
00:27:59.096 --> 00:28:01.265
-It's fine. Thank you for asking.
-<i>"And swallow you must,</i>

571
00:28:01.348 --> 00:28:04.059
<i>because Ted is out there in the community</i>

572
00:28:04.142 --> 00:28:07.855
<i>either bravely
or stupidly facing the music."</i>

573
00:28:07.938 --> 00:28:10.023
-Hey, fellas. How you doing?
-<i>"That's for you to decide."</i>

574
00:28:10.107 --> 00:28:11.859
Piss off, wanker!

575
00:28:13.819 --> 00:28:15.404
-Hi.
-Yeah.

576
00:28:15.487 --> 00:28:17.030
-Stop it.
-Every time.

577
00:28:17.114 --> 00:28:19.408
<i>"And yes, he's in over his head.</i>

578
00:28:19.491 --> 00:28:23.704
<i>He insisted twice that he didn't care
if Richmond won or lost.</i>

579
00:28:23.787 --> 00:28:28.250
<i>But if the Lasso way is wrong,
it's hard to imagine being right."</i>

580
00:28:30.794 --> 00:28:32.129
Why have you stopped reading?

581
00:28:33.297 --> 00:28:37.176
Please do me the favor of remembering that
these aren't my words, it's Trent Crimm.

582
00:28:38.051 --> 00:28:39.052
Keep going.

583
00:28:40.262 --> 00:28:42.514
-"In a business that celebrates ego,
-<i>...celebrates ego,</i>

584
00:28:42.598 --> 00:28:43.974
-Ted reins his in."
-<i>Ted reins his in.</i>

585
00:28:44.057 --> 00:28:48.478
<i>His coaching style is subtle.
It never hits you over the head.</i>

586
00:28:48.562 --> 00:28:51.607
Hello, Roy.
I didn't know it was a retirement party.

587
00:28:53.817 --> 00:28:54.818
Shit!

588
00:28:55.319 --> 00:28:56.570
Stop messing with Nate!

589
00:28:57.321 --> 00:28:58.780
Now, I don't know
which one of you I nutted,

590
00:28:58.864 --> 00:29:00.240
'cause I don't
see so well at night anymore,

591
00:29:00.324 --> 00:29:01.366
but that goes for all of you!

592
00:29:02.159 --> 00:29:05.996
<i>Slowly growing until you can no longer
ignore its presence.</i>

593
00:29:06.914 --> 00:29:08.081
Vanilla vodka.

594
00:29:09.291 --> 00:29:10.292
Such a child.

595
00:29:12.669 --> 00:29:13.795
Keeley.

596
00:29:13.879 --> 00:29:14.880
Roy.

597
00:29:15.506 --> 00:29:18.342
<i>Whether that means
allowing followers to become leaders,</i>

598
00:29:20.093 --> 00:29:23.305
<i>or in a show of respect,
eating food so spicy</i>

599
00:29:23.388 --> 00:29:26.558
<i>it's sure to wreak massive havoc
on his intestinal system.</i>

600
00:29:26.642 --> 00:29:27.935
Keys, keys, keys.

601
00:29:28.018 --> 00:29:30.020
Okay, here we go. Oh boy. Oh boy.

602
00:29:30.103 --> 00:29:32.773
<i>And though I believe that
Ted Lasso will fail here</i>

603
00:29:32.856 --> 00:29:35.901
<i>and Richmond will suffer
the embarrassment of relegation,</i>

604
00:29:37.027 --> 00:29:38.862
<i>I won't gloat when it happens.</i>

605
00:29:40.030 --> 00:29:42.074
<i>Because I can't help but root for him.</i>

606
00:29:43.700 --> 00:29:45.327
Fuck!

